\title{An execution that sends the order's whole quantity as one broker order, which is UBI's default}
\description{
The \code{all_at_once} execution of a plan: the whole quantity sent as one broker order.

This is what UBI does when an order names no execution, so it is needed only to say so explicitly, or to replace an execution an earlier preset gave. Under a join that changes how much the order should trade, the one resting order is modified rather than another being sent, so a bracket's exits grow and shrink in place. It is one of the two executions a resting stop may have, the other being \code{DailyExecution}.
}
